Docker

What is docker?
Docker is a platform that packages an application and everything it needs (code, libraries, runtime, configuration) into a container
so it runs the same way on any computer.


Why Docker is Needed
Docker provides:
-Same environment everywhere
-Easy application deployment
-Isolation between applications
-Fast startup
-Lightweight compared to Virtual Machines

Docker packages:Application, Runtime, Libraries, Dependencies, Configuration into a Docker Image.
When that image runs, it becomes a Docker Container.

Docker Architecture:
               Docker Client
          (docker run, docker build)
                     │
                     ▼
             Docker Engine (Daemon)
                     │
      ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
      ▼                             ▼
 Docker Images               Docker Containers

1)Docker Client:
  This is what you use.
  Example: docker run nginx or docker build
  The client sends commands to Docker Engine.

2. Docker Engine (Daemon)
This is the brain of Docker.
It:
-Builds images
-Creates containers
-Starts containers
-Stops containers
-Deletes containers
-Downloads images

3. Docker Image:
A Docker image is the template used to create containers.
  An Image is a read-only blueprint.
    It contains : Application, Libraries, Runtime, Configuration

Example: Python, Flask, requirements.txt, app.py
  Together these become one image.

4.Docker Container:
A Container is a running instance of an image.
  Example: Employee API Container
    Running.
  Another: Employee API Container
    Running.
    Both came from the same image.

| Command                       | Creates Container | Starts Container            |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------- |
| `docker run nginx`            | ✅ Yes             | ✅ Yes                       |
| `docker create nginx`         | ✅ Yes             | ❌ No                        |
| `docker start container-name` | ❌ No              | ✅ Starts existing container |

Container ఒక image ఆధారంగా create అవుతుంది. docker run అనేది create చేసి start చేస్తుంది; docker create అనేది create మాత్రమే చేస్తుంది.

IMAGE = Docker local storage లో ఉంటుంది
          ↓ used by
CONTAINER = Docker create చేసి manage చేసే running/stopped instance

How Docker Runs an Application
-------------------------------
Suppose you have: Employee REST API
Step 1 : Write the code.
app.py

Step 2 : Create a Dockerfile.
  FROM python:3.12
  COPY . .
  RUN pip install -r requirements.txt
  CMD ["python","app.py"]

Step 3 : Build an image.
docker build -t employee-api .
  Docker creates: employee-api image

Step 4 : Run the image.
  docker run employee-api and Docker creates a container.
Inside that container: Python, Flask, Libraries, Employee API
Everything starts automatically.


| Concept       | Meaning                               |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Docker        | Platform to create and run containers |
| Image         | Blueprint/template of an application  |
| Container     | Running instance of an image          |
| Dockerfile    | Instructions to build an image        |
| Docker Engine | Runs and manages containers           |
| Docker Hub    | Online repository of Docker images    |


